#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|title=Awsworth Neighbourhood Plan 2015-2030|passage=By 1765, rapid enclosure was underway in the surrounding area (open fields replaced by the modern system of private fields). By the time of the 1846 ‘Tithe Map and Award’ very little remained of the original agricultural system other than indications in field names, such as Ginn '''Close''', Straw '''Close''', Crab Tree '''Close''', Noble '''Close''', Tinker '''Close''', Laine '''Close''', Hansack '''Close''', Hansacky, Little Hansacky, The Pringle and Dole Meadow. (Note – ‘'''Close'''’ meaning an enclosure).|author=Michael Smith|page=14|line=2.12|publisher=Awsworth Parish Council|location=Awsworth, Notts, UK|edition_plain=Adopted Version, July 2021|format=PDF|
url=https://www.awsworthparishcouncil.gov.uk/community/neighbourhood-plan|author2=Stuart Lee|author3=Lydia Ball|author4=David Bamford|author5=Don Foster|author6=John Mortimer|author7=Richard Paxton|author8=Carol Sanderson|author9=Dawn Savage|author10=Graham Spencer|author11=James Woodward|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260630132911/https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/68544504824b969882ceb982/68f3d7bb1d7cab8b13102c62_awsworth-neighbourhood-plan-adopted-final-s%20(1).pdf|archivedate=30/06/2026}}
